  "notes": "USAGE:\n{託|たく}す is a godan verb (Group I) that implies entrusting something with emotional significance. It differs from {預|あず}ける (to leave in someone's care physically) in that {託|たく}す carries a more abstract, often lofty sense — entrusting hopes, dreams, or important missions. The pattern ～に{思|おも}いを{託|たく}す (to put one's feelings/wishes into something) is very common.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {夢|ゆめ}を{託|たく}す: to entrust one's dream to\n- {期待|きたい}を{託|たく}す: to place one's expectations on\n- {思|おも}いを{託|たく}す: to put one's feelings into\n- {後|あと}を{託|たく}す: to leave what follows to someone",
